''We’ve updated World 345, the permanent Deadman world! Introducing new charms, reimagined PvP mechanics, and the return of boss breaches.''

==Changelog March 12th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Permanent Deadman W345 Updates'''

* Added four new charms, obtained from killing NPCs at 200 combat level or higher:
** Nimbleness Charm: Boosts Marks of Grace drops from one to five, lets you bypass Agility level requirement restrictions on shortcuts, and auto re-pickpockets NPCs.
** Stockpiling Charm: Triples rewards from Wintertodt, Tempoross, and Guardians of the Rift, stacks Clue Scroll drops, and auto-Banks skilling resources.
** Accumulation Charm: Triples Clue Scroll drops, Chinchompa captures, and skilling resources, and provides 5x Runecraft yields.
** Vulnerability Charm: Increases Accuracy against monsters by 50%, multiplies Thrall Max Hits by 5, and cuts incoming monster damage by 25%.
* Boss breaches now appear on weekends!
** Both area and specific location breaches will occur, just as in Deadman Armageddon.
*** Up to 25 NPCs spawn in area breaches, and up to 6 NPCs spawn in specific location ones. They'll be dropping:
**** Ancient Warrior Weapons
**** Trinkets previously seen in Deadman: Armageddon
**** New charms (although you've mostly seen their effects in previous Deadman events)
** Sigils and corrupted weapons remain off-limits.
** If you have protection still, you will not be able to attack any breach NPCs, both in single and multi-combat zones.
** Each breach monster drops one Chitin per kill with a 50% chance for a bonus supply drop instead.
** Weekend breaches will occur every four hours, starting on Saturday at 02:00 GMT. The last breach will be on Sunday at 22:00 GMT.
** You’ll get a timely notification in your chat when a breach goes live. You can also talk to Perdu to see where the breach is and how long it will be around for.
* Combat brackets are now divided into Levels 3–75, 76–85, and 86+ with a 2x unique drop rate modifier for each bracket.
* The PJ Timer now follows a last-hit system. Land that final blow to trigger an uninterrupted teleport, or risk having your escape cut off by a sneaky PKer.
* When PKed, attackers now only grab 50% of your top 10 stackable items.
* Added supply drop tables from Deadman: Armageddon.
* Wilderness Slayer Tasks now yield both Tier 1 and Tier 5 Emblems.
* Changes to Morrigan’s Javelin Special:
** The bleed effect triggers every tick (down from every three ticks) with damage boosted from 5 to 10 per tick.
** Total bleed equals 75% of your original hit (e.g. a 40-damage hit produces three bleed splats of 10 each).
* Buffed Morrigan’s Thrownaxe: Now only consumes 25% special attack. A successful hit speeds up your next attack by 1 tick, making it a slick 3-tick attack on rapid.
* Classic Content Returns:
** Giant seaweed runs on Fossil Island are back!
** Frog random events now stick around.
** “Crack the Clue 3” can be completed.
* Bounty Hunter Shop Additions:
** Imbue Scroll: 1,000,000 points.
** Castle Wars Halos: 500,000 points each.
** Trouver Parchment: 250,000 points.
* QoL changes:
** Players can now receive regular loot from Revenants, though Emblem drops remain disabled.
** For skulled players, an Emblem drop roll yields either Magic or Yew Seeds; unskulled players receive a Dragon Med Helm.
** Players now receive double Dragon Bones and Superior Dragon Bones from Green and Black Dragons and Vorkath. Both Dragon Bones will be noted in the Wilderness if you've completed the Wilderness Elite Diary Tier.
** Pest Control now awards 4x the points, and the Agility Pyramid now grants 30,000 coins instead of 10,000.
** Blighted Overloads are now available in Permanent Deadman - craft them with Super Combat, Magic, and Ranging Potions, a Deadman Overload Chitin, and a dash of 83 Herblore.
** Statius’s Warhammer now guarantees a hit on Tekton’s first Special Attack and doubles as a regular hammer for building chests in Chambers.
** Players can no longer enter the Colosseum or create a private instance at the Hueycoatl while skulled.
** Chat with Nigel at the Lumbridge graveyard or use a Deadman chest to toggle off Combat XP, or just Hitpoints XP individually, if you wish.

'''Other Changes''' 

* Fixed an issue where POH telescopes using the Civitas or Canifis wallkits would incorrectly display a message about the wall instead of showing incoming Shooting Stars. They will now function as intended, allowing stargazers to track Shooting Star landings properly.
* The following items can now properly access charge configuration:
** Crystal Halberd, Bow, and Shield: All three now share the same "Quantity" variable, and use Crystal charges, not coins.
** Echo Venator Bow
** Alchemist’s Amulet
** Celestial Ring and Signet
** Giantsoul Amulet
** Pendant of Ates
* Upon creating Emberlight, Scorching Bow, and Purging Staff from the Tormented Synapse, you will now receive the original 730 Smithing, Fletching, or Crafting XP for the first upgrade, followed by 73 XP every time after.
* During a Hell-Rat Behemoth fight, you can now use Fish and Milk directly on your cat to support it, rather than having to pass them through the alcove's curtain.
* Reanimated goblins can now drop the Champions' Challenge Scroll.

'''PvP Rota '''
The PvP rota has moved to '''Period B''':

* 560 - (UK) - PvP World
* 319 - (US) - Bounty Hunter World
* 579 - (US) - High-Risk PvP World
* 561 - (UK) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 580 - (US) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using ''''1 Def Pure'''' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

